\section*{Impact Statement}
This work aims to reduce the cost, phototoxicity, and reagent use of fluorescence microscopy by generating virtual stains from label-free images. This can accelerate high-content screening and make advanced imaging more accessible in resource-limited labs. Because downstream biological conclusions may rely on the fidelity of virtual stains, inaccurate predictions could mislead research or clinical workflows if used uncritically. We therefore advocate reporting rigorous benchmarks so that users can assess reliability in their own settings before deployment.
