	The cycles $\gamma_1, \gamma_2$ (resp. $\gamma_3, \gamma_4$) originate from marked boundary vertices (resp. trivalent vertices). Notice that for every cycle, all weights are equal to $1$, so in this example they are (unweighted) subgraphs of the weave. Also notice that all $4$ cycles are frozen.%We separated cycle $\gamma_3$ from other cycles so that there are no overlaps between cycles. 
