		\item Let $\ww': \rho \rev{{T^{+}}} \rarrow \rev{T^{+}}$ be a decorated Demazure weave with the top word $\rho \rev{T^{+}}$ decorated from $\mch$ to $\mcg$ such that the decoration for $\rev{T^+}$ is $\rev{\dec_T}(\mck, \mcg)$. Then the decoration for the bottom word is the reversed normalized decoration $\rev{\dec_T}(\mch, \mcg)$.Moreover, the seed $\seed(\ww')$ does not depend on the choice of the Demazure weave $\ww'$. 
