\begin{lemma}\label{Kz}
Suppose that $v\in F_X\cap\cK$.  Then $(v,T)\sim(v,T')$ if and only if $\cK_{X,T} = \cK_{X,T'}$.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Both conditions are equivalent to the statement that the chambers $F_T$ and $F_{T'}$ lie on the same side of every hyperplane containing $v$.
\end{proof}
