The neodymium measurements have higher contaminant peaks. We believe this is due to vacuum conditions and outgassing of O-rings and have identified a path forward to reduce the contaminants further.
% Note, for example, that the \hthreep fraction is lower in the neodymium cases than in the \smco case. Thus, for the comparison plot, we elected to show the \htp fraction of hydrogen species. 
In addition to displaying the fractional results, FIG.~\ref{fig:magnet-study-res} corroborates the findings in Ref.~\cite{winklehnerHighcurrentH2Beams2021a} that increased gas flow leads to a higher \hthreep fraction and that discharge voltage seems to have a minimal effect on ion species fractions.

