Our main contributions are as follows. We introduce a general prototype class of {\it consistent-non-sparse  and unpenalized} precision matrix estimators based on a deep connection between matrix algebra and hidden factor analysis. Hidden factor analysis is used only for achieving consistency in high dimensions via dimension reduction. Our estimators are model-free, and do not need to estimate hidden factors.
