	\begin{assum}\label{as1}
	(i). $y_{jt}, Y_{-jt}$ are iid across $t=1,\cdots, n$ for each $j=1,\cdots,p$.

	(ii). $u_{jt}, U_{-jt}$ are zero mean random variable and vector respectively, which are iid across $t=1,\cdots,n$,  for each $j=1,\cdots,p$.

	(iii). $f_t$ are iid across $t=1,\cdots, n$.

	(iv). $f_t, u_{jt}, U_{-jt}$ are mutually independent across $t=1,\cdots,n $ given $j=1,\cdots,p$.

