\subsubsection{Adaptive PCR Estimator}\label{apcr}

 In case of adaptive PCR, the random terms in the upper bound in Theorem \ref{thm1}, can be bounded  as:  $\bar{r} \le K$ wpa1, $\bar{\Psi}/\bar{\eta} \le1$ wpa1, $\bar{\eta} \ge \delta_n$ with wpa1. So Theorem \ref{thm1} rate can be simplified in adaptive PCR, 
with $\hat{\Theta}_{PCR,j}'$ representing the estimator of $j$ th row of $\Theta$.  The following Corollary follows from Theorem \ref{thm1} by replacing $r_{w1}, r_{w2}$ with 
$r_{w1,PCR}, r_{w2, PCR}$ rates that are shown before Corollary OA.1 in Online Appendix.



\begin{corollary}\label{cl4}


