& \le & \max_{1 \le j \le p} \| a_j \|_2 \sqrt{K p} \max_{1 \le j \le p} \| \frac{1}{n} \sum_{t=1}^n f_t U_{-jt}'\|_{\infty} \nonumber \\
& = & O (\sqrt{K})  O_p ( \frac{\sqrt{K p (logp)}}{\sqrt{n}}) = O_p ( K \sqrt{p} \frac{\sqrt{logp}}{\sqrt{n}}),\label{62}
\end{eqnarray}
where we use for the first inequality (\ref{i1})
and then for the second inequality we use (\ref{61}) and for the rates we use Assumption \ref{as5}(iii), and Lemma 2.7.7 and Corollary 2.8.3 of \cite{v2019} with Assumption \ref{as4} since $f_t U_{-jt}'$ is $K \times p-1$ matrix.  Then for the fourth term on the right side of (\ref{58}) via Corollary 2.8.3 of \cite{v2019} and Assumption \ref{as4}
