We start this section about examples with the class of graphs whose magneto-spectral height vanishes.

\begin{lemma} \label{lem:treenu}
Any magnetic potential can be gauged away if and only if $G=(V,E)$ is a forest. Therefore,
we have $\nu(G)=0$ if and only if $G$ is a forest.
\end{lemma}

