The following result states that our lower bound for $\nu(W_d)$ is sharp.

\begin{proposition} \label{prop:wheelnu}
For any wheel graph $W_d$, $d\geq 3$, we have
\begin{equation} \label{eq:nuWdnuCd}
    \nu(W_{d})=\nu(C_{d})+1 = 3-2\cos(\pi/d).
\end{equation}
\end{proposition}
\begin{proof}
We apply Theorem \ref{thm:outdegree_upper_bound} in Section \ref{sec:genresults} below to wheel graphs, by choosing $G=(V,E)$ as $W_d$ and the subgraph $G_0=(V_0,E_0)$ as the cycle $C_d$. Then we obtain the inequality:
$$ \nu(W_d) \le \nu(C_d)+1. $$
Combining this with the results in Example \ref{ex:wheel} and Example \ref{ex:cycle} completes the proof of the proposition.
% Combining this inequality with inequalities \eqref{eq:w_2k+1_larger}, \eqref{eq:w_2k_larger} in the above yields the equality \eqref{eq:nuWdnuCd} for wheel graphs.
\end{proof}

