\begin{question}\label{quest:nu_degree}
Proposition \ref{prop:combupbd} below states that $\nu(G)$ is bounded above by the average vertex degree 
$$ \frac{1}{|V|} \sum_{x \in V} d_x = \frac{2|E|}{|V|}. $$
It is therefore natural to ask, whether $\nu(G)$ is also bounded below  by the average degree of a graph $G$, that is, whether there exist a universal constant $c >0$ such that 
\begin{equation} \label{eq:nuaverdeg}
\frac{c}{|V|}\sum_{x\in V}d_x\leq \nu(G).
\end{equation}
Example \ref{ex:avverdeg} answers this question negatively.
\end{question}

