\section{General results}
\label{sec:genresults}
% {\color{red} Bobo's result works for arbitrary subgraphs and involves the maximum of the out-degrees. In the case of tree subgraphs, one can apply Phil's isoperimetric result and can improve the maximal out-degree by the average out-degree. If we choose cycle subgraphs, the improvement to average out-degree still works since the complex eigenfunction to the smallest eigenvalue for all magnetic potentials is unimodular. In general, if this is the case for a subgraph, maximum of out-degree can be improved to average out-degree. }


\subsection{Upper combinatorial bounds}

We start this section with a combinatorial upper bound of the magneto-spectral height of a graph $G=(V,E)$. To formulate it, we recall that the \emph{first Betti number} $b_1(G)$ of $G$ is given by $|E|-|V|+k$, where $k$ is the number of connected components of $G$. Note that $b_1(G)$ is also called the \emph{dimension of the cycle space}.
We have the following three upper combinatorial bounds.

\begin{proposition} \label{prop:combupbd}
    Let $G=(V,E)$ be a graph. Then we have
    $$ \nu(G) \le \min\left\{ \frac{2|E|}{|V|}, \frac{4b_1(G)}{|V|}, %|V|-2, 
    d_{\max}-1 \right\},$$
    where $d_{\max}$ is the maximal vertex of degree of $G$.
\end{proposition}

\begin{remark}
All three upper bounds in this proposition are relevant. Note that the upper bound $\frac{2|E|}{|V|}$ is the average vertex degree of the graph $G=(V,E)$. Figure \ref{fig:firstandsecondgraph} illustrates examples of graphs $G$ for which we have
$$ \frac{2|E|}{|V|} = \frac{2(2n-1)}{n} < \min\left\{\frac{4b_1(G)}{|V|}, d_{\max}-1\right\}, $$
(since $n \ge 6$, $\frac{4b_1(G)}{|V|}=4$ and $d_{\max}=n-2$)
and
$$ \frac{4b_1(G)}{|V|} = \frac{4(e-n+1)}{n} < \min\left\{\frac{2|E|}{|V|},d_{\max}-1\right\}, $$
(since $n \ge 5$, $e=|E|=2n-3$, $\frac{2|E|}{|V|}=4-\frac{6}{n}$ and
$d_{\max}=n-2$), respectively. Examples of graphs for which we have
$$ d_{\max}-1 < \min
\left\{\frac{2|E|}{|V|},\frac{4b_1(G)}{|V|}\right\}, $$
are all $d$-regular connected graphs with $d \ge 3$. 

