\section{Summary and Outlook}\label{sec:outllok}
The work estimated antenna orientations at the prototype station surface array enhancement of IceCube Observatory by quantifying the galactic signal strength measurements and looking for their modulation as a function of the azimuth of Galactic center. The final obtained orientation measurements from data are in good agreement with GPS measurements on yearly basis. The agreement with GPS measurements indicates that this method is a promising approach for determining antenna orientation. Ongoing work to improve the various cleaning and filtering methods may potentially allow for a more frequent estimate of antenna orientations using galactic noise.     
