 \widetilde{\widetilde{m}}(g) = \frac{3}{\pi} \int_{A(g_x, g_y) \cap \mathcal{F}} \frac{1}{y^2} \, \dd x \, \dd y,
\]
where $A(g_x,g_y)$ is the region in the upper half-plane defined by
\[
A(g_x, g_y) = \left\{ x + i y \in \mathcal{H} : x + g_x y > -\frac{1}{2} \text{ and } \left( x + g_x y + 1 \right)^2 + \left( g_y y \right)^2 > 1 \right\}
