The region $A(g_x, g_y)$ is the intersection of the area outside the ellipse $E(x,y): (x + g_x y + 1)+(g_y y)^2=1$ and the one side of the line $L(x,y): x+g_x y=-\frac{1}{2}$. The region $A(g_x,g_y)\cap \mathcal{F}$, depicted in Figure \ref{fig: A cap F}, represents the overlapped area determined by a parameterized ellipse, a line, and the fundamental domain $\mathcal{F}$. \par 

