	Building on the identified reciprocal reinforcement mechanism between fracture evolution and wetting-enhanced diffusion dynamics, we next analyze the experimental and simulation results for Sample-2, where extended cycling leads to the formation of more severe cracks. A new sectioned single-crystal lamellae, with FIB-generated center hole and surrounding Pt frame, is shown in Figure~\ref{fig:new-sample} (a) and (b) from front and top perspectives, respectively.
