Abstract
This work concerns with the existence of traveling wave solutions for the following
difusive predator–prey type system with Holling type-III functional response:
where all parameters are positive which will be mentioned later. The traveling wave
solutions are established in R4
, which is a heteroclinic orbit connecting the boundary equilibrium and the positive equilibrium. Applying the methods of Wazewski
Theorem and LaSalle’s Invariance Principle, and constructing a Liapunov function,
we obtain the existence of traveling wave solutions. We also discuss some possible
biological implications of the existence of these waves.

